 "schema": "kerbside.validation.habs-front-wall/1",
 "date": "2026-10-13",
 "what": "The blind HABS test scored on the main front wall only -- what the pipeline infers -- and on the one photograph the house is rendered from.",
 "scope": "Scored on the main front wall only, as the pipeline infers it: an opening drawn above the wall's top (a dormer, a tower attic, above the cornice) is the roof's, and one inside a wing's span (truth.wings_u, read from the drawing) is that wing's wall. Predicted openings there are set aside the same way.",
 "source": "Historic American Buildings Survey (Library of Congress), public domain; scans from the Library of Congress and its Wikimedia Commons mirror; building footprints (c) OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL); heights from USGS 3D Elevation Program lidar (public domain). Photographs, drawings and lidar tiles were deleted after scoring; only these numbers are kept.",
 "method": [
  "Every count is of one front: the elevation drawing of the side the photographs show, never the other sides. Of the 113 openings drawn on those fronts, 26 are set aside here as not the main front wall: 13 dormers and tower-attic windows above the wall's top, and 13 on wings with walls of their own (Stanford's west wing, the Governor's Mansion's east wing, Larkin's stone wing, J. S. Cain's rear wing). Predicted openings in the same places are set aside alike. 87 remain.",
  "The house is rendered from one photograph -- the one the frontage filter picks (within 40 degrees, nearest square on, the house filling the frame) -- and only that photograph's openings are scored. The pipeline now uses the other photographs only for depth (stairs, alcoves; smc.facades.multiview), which the drawings do not record; the earlier runs' fusion of several photographs is gone.",
  "Otherwise as the lidar run: given one to three photographs, the OpenStreetMap footprint (width) and 3DEP lidar (height); the house found by Grounding DINO; the pipeline unchanged. A match: centres within max(1.5 m, the opening's size) and IoU >= 0.1.",
  "A diagnostic run, not blind, gives the same photograph the drawing's own width and height."
 ],
