 "findings": [
  "On the main front wall alone: 15 of 87 openings found (17%), and 56% of what was predicted there is real. Counted over the whole drawn elevation, the same photographs score 16 of 113 (14%, 43% real): scoping to the front lifts precision, since 10 predictions had landed on wings and roofs, but not recall.",
  "The gap is how few openings are proposed: 27 for 87. The large many-bayed fronts get almost none -- Stanford 3 for 23, the Governor's Mansion 4 for 22, Amesti 2 for 11 -- where a window is about forty pixels wide in the scan and the pixel screen flags vegetation across the front.",
  "What is proposed is mostly right where the front is clear: Larkin 6 of 9 found with all 6 predictions real; J. S. Cain's one prediction real.",
  "Given the drawing's own width and height (not blind) it is still 15 of 87: size is not the gap; the detector's recall on archival photographs is."
 ]
